    "narrative": "Our lineup today is anchored by **Seiya Suzuki**, whose score of 75.03 makes him our premier start. **Seiya Suzuki** benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against Andrew Abbott, where a favorable park factor and a +19% SP skill advantage significantly elevate his output. Similarly, **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.92) is in a prime position to produce; he draws a +16% park adjustment and a +14% platoon advantage against Shane Baz, making him a high-floor play in the UTIL spot. We are also looking for high-upside speed contributions from **Mickey Moniak** (68.98) and **Corbin Carroll** (66.61). **Mickey Moniak** is particularly intriguing against Trevor McDonald due to his propensity to exploit slow deliveries, while **Corbin Carroll** remains an auto-start despite facing a tougher arm in Emmet Sheehan, simply due to his elite ceiling in the scarce stolen base category.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Kyle Karros**, who scored 45.71 but ultimately fell short of our high-efficiency threshold. While **Kyle Karros** benefits from the same slow-delivery environment that aids **Mickey Moniak**, his projected #5 spot in the lineup lacks the run-production pressure of the top-of-order bats, and the optimizer prioritized the higher-leverage platoon advantages offered by our starters. We are monitoring the status of **Gabriel Moreno**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Brice Turang**, **Alex Freeland**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Austin Riley**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **James Wood**, all of whom are currently tagged with \"Lineup Pending.\" While **James Wood** (64.45) looks like a lock for production given his elite .434 xwOBA, we are exercising caution with **Brice Turang** (47.98), who faces the formidable Paul Skenes; the risk of a sub-optimal day is high here, but his value in stolen bases keeps him on the field. We are holding **Jose Caballero**, **Josh Naylor**, and **Edwin Arroyo** in reserve to maintain our daily game cap efficiency, ready to pivot should any late lineup scratches emerge.",
